      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no scientifically validated evidence that correlates the use of non-standard vernaculars with a student's inherent cognitive discipline or academic readiness. Linguistic patterns reflect cultural background and community, not intellectual capacity. Focusing on measurable skills, such as critical thinking assessments and demonstrated aptitude in coursework, will provide a much more accurate measure for your admissions criteria.",
